 "description": "Experiment record (issue #130): fills the 56 previously missing reachable-pair reference counts of flpq_data/dataset/reachable_pairs.csv. The in-archive results.mtx stubs of these pairs were empty placeholders; each was computed with FastMatrixCFPQ 1.1.0 (IncrementalAllPairsCFLReachabilityMatrix) on a 24-core / 124 GB RAM host, using the language-equivalent low-memory grammar where one exists (c_alias_muravev2024.cnf, java_points_to_muravev2024.cnf, and the task-157 sparse uniprot grammar unigraph_1_sparse.cnf) and recorded under the canonical in-archive grammar name. The repacked archives with filled results.mtx were uploaded to 6.0.0/graph/<graph>.tar.gz and audited (sha256 + structure, 50/50 OK). 48 computed counts match the independent references of temporal_cfpq/results/reference_answers.csv exactly; the 8 java_points_to pairs with stale references were confirmed correct by the user (issue #130). The remaining 4 pairs are documented infeasible on this hardware.",
